<!--
    kuna GH-181: an out-parameter copy hoisted ABOVE the call that fills it.

    The function is libselinux lsetfilecon_raw (x86-64 gcc -O2, stripped;
    tests/bug-repro/libselinux.so.1 at 0x17370).  The source idiom:

        char *ccontext = NULL;
        if ((lgetfilecon_raw(path, &amp;ccontext) >= 0) &amp;&amp;
            (strcmp(context, ccontext) == 0)) { rc = 0; } else { errno = err; }
        freecon(ccontext);

    The binary loads the stack slot ONCE, after the call returns, and both
    strcmp and freecon consume that post-call value.  kuna instead emitted

        v4 = NULL;
        v1 = v4;                                  (copy BEFORE the call)
        if ((0 &lt;= (int4)lgetfilecon_raw(a0,&amp;v4)) ...
        freecon(v1);                              (frees the pre-call NULL)

    which as C frees NULL and leaks the buffer the call allocated.

    Two stacked defects, both correctness fixes with no option:

    1. Stage S6 variable merge, cover-trim insertion (p6_variables/merge.rs
       Merge::snip_reads via substrate/funcdata.rs do_snip_reads_insert_point).
       Upstream Merge::snipReads (decompiler/cpp/merge.cc:461) has an explicit
       carve-out: when the trimmed Varnode is defined by a CPUI_INDIRECT, the
       trim COPY is inserted after the op CAUSING the effect (the iop encoding
       in the INDIRECT's input 1), not at the INDIRECT itself, which precedes
       the call in block order.  The kuna port lacked the INDIRECT arm, so the
       COPY feeding freecon landed before the CALL in the p-code.

    2. The kuna-only foldcallret fold (p6_variables/kuna_callretfold.rs,
       default-on per DIV-14) sank the call expression into the if condition
       across that COPY: an op reading a value the call indirectly writes (an
       input defined by a CPUI_INDIRECT attached to the call) is now a fold
       barrier, since moving the call text past it hands it the pre-call value.

    Two passes: pass 1 default (foldcallret on) proves both fixes together;
    pass 2 (option foldcallret off, the upstream-faithful rendering) proves the
    p-code level snip_reads fix alone.  Both passes must show the corrected
    ordering: the call statement first, the out-parameter copy directly after
    it, never a slot copy immediately preceding the call text.
-->
